    "Id": "vehicledef_THUNDERER_II",
    "Name": "Thunderer II MT",
    "Details": "Created by a Capellan Confederation design team, the Thunderer was rushed into production during the chaos of the 4th succession war. Originally intended as a heavy tank to anchor second line formations and support infantry, the tank made a name for itself as a capable sniper that could harass and kill Mechs. The MK2 Thunderer mounts 12 tons of armour and is built around a 165 rated fusion engine. Mounted in the turret are an ER PPC and a UAC/5 with a hull mounted Machine Gun providing additional firepower.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: None.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 3/5 hexes / 90/150 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Armor\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       230     30\n<b>Left</b>         155     30\n<b>Right</b>       155     30\n<b>Rear</b>        140     30\n<b>Turret</b>      210     30\n\n<b>Total</b>      890    150</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Improved Targeting - Long</color>",
    "Icon": "Zhukov"
  },
